APXF["za-worcester"] = {"lede": "The Worcester district is the brandy capital of South Africa, with the largest distillery of its kind in the Southern Hemisphere, and a major source of bulk and branded wine.", "facts": [["Category", "WO"], ["Recognized", ""], ["Main grapes", "Chenin Blanc, Colombard, Shiraz, Muscadel"]], "sections": [["The place", "<p>It has seven wards: Hex River Valley, Keeromsberg, Moordkuil, Nuy, Rooikrans, Scherpenheuvel and Stettyn.</p>"], ["The rules", "<p>A Wine of Origin production area. South Africa's Wine of Origin scheme came into force in 1973 and now operates under the Liquor Products Act of 1989, administered by the Wine and Spirit Board. The law defines a hierarchy of geographical units (such as Western Cape), regions, districts and wards, plus registered single vineyards; overarching units such as Cape Coast and Greater Cape allow blends across regions. A ward must have a clear influence of soil, climate and ecology on the wine, and its name must reflect a real geographic feature. 'Wine of Origin' with an area name guarantees that 100% of the grapes come from that area; a variety or vintage on the label requires 85%. The certification seal on the bottle confirms that the claims were checked and the wine passed tasting. The scheme sets no rules on grapes, yields or style.</p>"], ["History", "<p>Worcester is the brandy capital of South Africa, with the KWV House of Brandy; South African brandy is double pot-distilled and aged in oak. Large cooperatives produce much of the country's volume.</p>"], ["In the glass", "<p>Brandy base, fortified Muscadel and good-value Chenin and Colombar.</p>"], ["For the exam", "<p>Brandy capital; cooperatives; Breede River Valley.</p>"]], "producers": ["Nuy", "Stettyn", "Alvi's Drift"], "sources": [["Wines of South Africa: Wine of Origin scheme", "https://www.wosa.co.za/The-Industry/Wines-Of-Origin/Wine-Of-Origin-scheme"], ["Wine Certification Authority: What we do", "https://wineauthority.org/what-we-do"], ["SAWIS: Wine of Origin Scheme (Liquor Products Act 60 of 1989), updated 2025", "https://www.sawis.co.za/winelaw/download/Wine_of_Origin_Scheme,_updated_05_2025.pdf"]], "checked": "2026-11-14"};
